Created this file for the ec2 migration for that i have list out all the commands & their output as well. Please read it once,verify & execute the commands.
Here is the architecture like steps what i'm goint to follow like below
=================
Existing EC2
     ↓
terraform import
     ↓
Terraform state
     ↓
terraform plan                                     ## These are all the steps i have followed & executed...
     ↓
terraform apply                                   
     ↓
EC2 managed by Terraform
     ↓
terraform destroy
     ↓
EC2 terminated
==================
I have created a ec2 instance of ubuntu image named as "my-web-server" in aws console.
so, now i need to migrate it with terraform. for that i have created a files of terraform files names given below...
main.tf
variable.tf & 
variable.tfvars
so, now i have given all the files below.
=====================
main.tf      ===>
------
provider "aws" {
  region = var.aws_region
}

resource "aws_instance" "production_ubuntu" {
  ami           = var.ami_id
  instance_type = var.instance_type

  tags = {
    Name        = var.instance_name
    Environment = "production"
  }
}
==============
variable.tf        ===>
----------
variable "aws_region" {
  type = string
}

variable "ami_id" {
  type = string
}

variable "instance_type" {
  type = string
}

variable "instance_name" {
  type = string
}
===============
variable.tfvars    ===>
-----------
aws_region    = "ap-south-2"
ami_id        = <"ami-id">    ## give a ami-id
instance_type = "t3.micro"   ## Given a type of instance example i have given t3.micro
instance_name = "production-ubuntu"  ## give a instance name
================
